From 2f79b549ef40aeb31cb3af36cd92d8d12b9ba799 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Rajan <7121943+kvnloo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 04:00:57 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(agent): keep repeated computer_use key presses in
 same-turn dedup

Same-turn duplicate elimination drops a tool call whose (name, arguments)
pair already appeared in the assistant message. For computer_use key input
the repeat is the request: Tab, Tab moves focus twice. The second press was
removed before dispatch and before the assistant message was stored, so only
one Tab reached the backend and the model's history showed a single press.
Only a log warning recorded the drop.

Move the dedup helper out of the run_agent.py facade into
agent/tool_dispatch_helpers.py, beside the other per-tool dispatch tables,
and keep calls listed in _ORDER_SIGNIFICANT_ACTIONS, currently only
computer_use action=key. The check peels the tool_search tool_call bridge
because computer_use is in the default defer list, so a session on the
default config reaches it through tool_call. Every other duplicate is
still dropped, including a repeated computer_use click on the same element.

The new test drives a real AIAgent turn against the loopback fake provider
with the in-tree no-op computer_use backend, over both the bridge and the
direct tool form. On main the backend records one key press instead of two.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
